// endpoint_report_page_drawn.proto — ReportPageDrawn. PAGE section.
//
// A WORKSPACE'S WEB PAGE SAYS ITS CONVERSATION IS ON SCREEN. A workspace is
// open (OpenTabs) only once its session is served AND its page has drawn its
// conversation, and only the page knows when it has drawn. The page calls this
// once its conversation is drawn (the root feed's opening page applied and
// painted, or a refused open drawn in its place), and AGAIN every time its
// page stream re-attaches while drawn: a daemon that restarted after the page
// drew has no other way to learn it, and an open waiting on a page that drew
// before the daemon came up would otherwise wait forever.
//
// The fact belongs to the PAGE (its WatchPage connection): it stands while that
// connection stands, and the daemon forgets it when the connection ends.

